cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use discopt in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "discopt: a hybrid MINLP solver with a Rust core"
abstract: >-
  discopt is a hybrid Mixed-Integer Nonlinear Programming (MINLP) solver
  combining a Rust backend (in-house primal/dual simplex, branch-and-bound
  tree management, FBBT/presolve, the POUNCE automatic-differentiation
  tape), a numpy relaxation layer, and Python orchestration. It supports
  spatial branch-and-bound, McCormick and alphaBB relaxations,
  neural-network embedding, generalized disjunctive programming, and two
  NLP backends (POUNCE, cyipopt).
type: software
authors:
